From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:54:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 146/148] fix(refinery): port the batch lane to upstream's
 task-artifact lifecycle (gcp-fooz4)

f709abe5 (#245) made every verified close keep the source branch ("MUST NOT
delete") and run gc gastown task-artifact-cleanup, with the head's
artifact_source_sha and artifact_cleanup_state=pending captured before its
rebase. The port (a1f35244) covered merge-push.sh only. merge-batch.sh,
live on winnow (merge_batch_max=3), still deleted every landed member's
branch and the stack-time already-merged member's branch, never ran
cleanup, and never gave members an artifact proof. A left-open member then
reached the single-bead lane with no proof, and its cleanup blocked on
"missing artifact_source_sha", so merge-push exited 2 after closing it.

merge-batch.sh now:
- never deletes a member's source branch, in land or in stack;
- records each member's proof in land before the push, with the same keys
  and semantics as the rebase step's capture of the head
  (mb_capture_artifact_proof: capture origin/<branch> and arm pending when
  absent, never overwrite, re-arm pending otherwise). A proof that cannot
  be recorded stops land with 2 before anything lands. The stack-time
  already-merged member gets its proof right before its close;
- runs task-artifact cleanup after each member's verified close. A cleanup
  that does not converge is handled as direct_cleanup handles it: the
  member stays closed, its pending/blocked state stays, land ends 2 with a
  "did not converge" line, and the other members still close and clean
  up. stack cannot stop the head's lane (it always exits 0), so there a
  non-converging cleanup is a WARN, left for find-work's sweep.

A push that fails (2/3/5/6/7) now writes the members' artifact proof and
nothing else. That proof is exactly what the rebase step leaves on a head
whose push fails.

test_refinery_merge_batch.sh: the gc stub now runs the REAL
task-artifact-cleanup.sh (its --rig scoped bead calls reach the fixture),
and every bead has a real task worktree in the city's artifact namespace,
so cleanup's evidence matrix runs against the real origin. The head carries
the proof the rebase step captures; members must get theirs from
merge-batch.sh. Before this change: land-green, target-moved-once,
left-open-recovery and stack-already-landed failed on deleted branches and
missing cleanup, the push-failure cases on missing proof, and the
left-open recovery's merge-push exited 2 on "missing artifact_source_sha".
After: every case passes, including a new case_land_cleanup_blocked
(dirty worktree: blocked, member closed, land 2). 23 cases.

The formula's batch paragraph now names the cleanup arm of land's status 2.

